"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n      <section class=\"section\">\n        <div class=\"shell panel\">\n          <h2>Request Plumbing and Electrical Repairs for a Managed Property</h2>\n          <p>\n            Email maxinemaintenance.au@outlook.com or call 0413 477 667 with the\n            property address, work-order reference, occupant contact and issue\n            description.\n          </p>\n          <a class=\"button\" href=\"contact.html?service=property-management.html\">Contact Ellis Services Group</a>\n        </div>\n      </section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-4",
"kind": "rich",
"html": "\n      <section class=\"rich-band\">\n        <div class=\"shell\">\n          <span class=\"eyebrow\">For property managers and occupiers</span>\n          <h2>Rental and Strata Maintenance: Scope, Access and Approval</h2>\n          <div class=\"split\">\n            <div>\n              <p>\n                Maintenance requests move more easily when the property,\n                symptom, access arrangements and approval pathway stay together.\n                This is useful whether the request begins with an occupant, a\n                building manager or a portfolio team.\n              </p>\n              <p>\n                Describe what is happening at the property and contact Ellis Services Group. We assess hot-water and water-affected electrical concerns on site and confirm the qualified trade arrangements, repair scope and quote.\n              </p>\n              <ul class=\"topic-links\">\n                <li>\n                  <a\n                    href=\"insights-tenant-property-manager-maintenance-handover.html\"\n                    >Guide: maintenance handover</a\n                  >\n                </li>\n                <li>\n                  <a href=\"news-useful-property-work-order.html\"\n                    >News: useful work orders</a\n                  >\n                </li>\n                <li><a href=\"contact.html?service=property-management.html\">Start an enquiry</a></li>\n              </ul>\n            </div>\n            <picture data-responsive-media><source type=\"image/avif\" srcset=\"perth-property-service-responsive-480.avif 480w, perth-property-service-responsive-960.avif 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width:800px) calc(100vw - 80px), 560px\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"perth-property-service-responsive-480.webp 480w, perth-property-service-responsive-960.webp 960w\" sizes=\"(max-width:800px) calc(100vw - 80px), 560px\"\n              class=\"content-photo\"\n              src=\"perth-property-service.png\"\n              width=\"1536\"\n              height=\"1024\"\n              alt=\"Property manager and tradesperson reviewing a maintenance request\"\n            /></picture>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>" as TrustedHtml
},
{
"id": "section-5",
"kind": "faq",
"container": "\n      <section class=\"section\">\n        <div class=\"shell\">\n          <span class=\"eyebrow\">A practical handover</span>\n          <h2>Plumbing and Electrical Work Orders: Property, Fault and Approval</h2>\n          <div class=\"rich-grid\">\n            <article>\n              <h3>Property</h3>\n              <p>\n                Address, unit number, affected area and any strata or\n                common-property context that could shape access.\n              </p>\n            </article>\n            <article>\n              <h3>Issue</h3>\n              <p>\n                The occupant's observable description, when it began, current\n                condition and any safely taken photos.\n              </p>\n            </article>\n            <article>\n              <h3>Access & approval</h3>\n              <p>\n                On-site contact, availability, parking or entry notes,\n                work-order reference and the approval contact.\n              </p>\n            </article>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      <!-- site-intent:start --><div class=\"intent-content shell text-column\" data-site-intent><h2>Tenant Repair Reports and Property-Manager Approval</h2><p>For rental properties, strata and agency-managed premises, keep the original observation separate from the work instruction. Identify who may approve investigation, who may approve repairs, and whether a spending limit applies. Include the occupant contact and access arrangements without publishing keys, alarm codes or other private entry information.</p><p>A hot-water leak and failed bathroom lights can belong in one work order, but they are not one diagnosis. We confirm the relevant plumbing and electrical tasks and quote the agreed scope. For common-property concerns, identify the managing contact rather than assuming that the occupant can authorise shared-system work.</p><p>If the condition changes before the visit, update the request. Where you need completion notes, an itemised scope or a particular agency reference, specify that requirement when arranging the work; the required documentation should be agreed, not assumed.</p><ul class=\"intent-links\"><li><a href=\"plumbing.html\">Plumbing support for rentals and strata</a></li><li><a href=\"electrical.html\">Electrical maintenance requests</a></li><li><a href=\"insights-tenant-property-manager-maintenance-handover.html\">Tenant-to-manager handover checklist</a></li><li><a href=\"news-useful-property-work-order.html\">Writing an assessable work order</a></li><li><a href=\"smoke-alarm-maintenance-perth.html\">Smoke-alarm work for managed properties</a></li><li><a href=\"news-clearer-property-maintenance-enquiry.html\">Prepare the first maintenance enquiry</a></li><li><a href=\"toilet-installation-perth.html\">Toilet Installation &amp; Replacement Perth</a></li><li><a href=\"exhaust-fans-perth.html\">Bathroom Exhaust Fan Replacement Perth</a></li><li><a href=\"rcd-testing-perth.html\">RCD Testing &amp; Safety Switch Checks Perth</a></li></ul><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:0:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:0:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:1:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:1:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:2:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:2:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:3:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:3:answer}}</details><details><summary>{{ppp:faq:4:question}}</summary>{{ppp:faq:4:answer}}</details></div><!-- site-intent:end --></section>" as TrustedHtml,
